Fixes drills finding 1 and adds the console's client for the documents APIs. All tests go in scripts/test-logout-preview.js (placeholder from P3-SCAFFOLD); this item does not edit test-preview-overlay.js.

(1) app/api/admin/logout/route.js is wrapped in tenantHandler(…, {allowUnresolved:true}). Before revokeSessionByToken it resolves the actor with verifySession(token, 'merchant'), falling back to the bootstrap actor exactly as requireAdmin does, and calls new revokePreviewSessionsFor({actor}) in lib/preview-sessions.js: UPDATE preview_sessions SET revoked_at = ? WHERE tenant_id = ? AND created_by = ? AND revoked_at IS NULL. The response always clears PREVIEW_COOKIE and ADMIN_COOKIE with the attributes /api/preview sets (httpOnly, sameSite lax, path '/', secure in production, maxAge 0), in every mode. A missing table, no tenant or a DB error logs 'preview_logout_revoke_failed' and never blocks logout.
Known changes, recorded in the packet and for the owner: logout ends that actor's previews on every device; on a legacy store logout now also ends the Designer's preview (a re-login re-mints it).

(2) app/api/platform/logout/route.js: also clears _preview with the same attributes. Platform-created preview sessions live in each tenant's DB and are not revoked (they expire within the hour): a recorded known limit.

(3) New components/admin/editor/documentsApi.js, plain JS, node-testable, fetch injectable. It maps responses using lib/admin/documents-api-shapes.js (import it; do not restate shapes). call(op, args) never throws and returns:
- {ok:true, data};
- {conflict:true, code, current} for 409 DOCUMENT_CHANGED or PUBLISHED_ELSEWHERE (current carries updatedByName);
- {refused:true, code, message, other?, offer?} for other 409s;
- {issues, code, message, offer?} for 422;
- {needsRevision:true} for 428;
- {notBuilt:true} for 501;
- {error:true, code, message} for other 4xx/5xx, using the failure() words;
- {error:true, code:'NETWORK_ERROR', message} when fetch rejects.
sendKeepalive(op, args) uses fetch keepalive and returns false when the JSON body exceeds 60,000 bytes. startDocumentsPreview({showDesign}) posts {create:true} to /api/admin/preview-session, sets showDesign when asked, fetches previewUrl same-origin, and returns {sid, expiresAt} or a mapped error. setShowDesign(sid, on) wraps the existing showDesign call.

The legacy components/admin/cms/api.js is not changed.

The storefront side of the editor, preview only. Shopper HTML without console cookies stays byte-identical.

(1) lib/content/resolve.js documentsPreview returns {refused: reason} for a correctly signed token whose session is revoked, expired or not found. contentSource then serves live content with source.previewRefused = reason.

(2) Bridge mounting in app/(storefront)/layout.js:
- valid documents preview: the bridge with state {kind, sid, docs:{[id]: draftHash}, offline:[ids], skipped, designShown};
- refused preview: a minimal bar 'Your preview has ended, so you're seeing the live store.' with an Exit link to /api/preview?exit=1, and the bridge with {ok:false, reason};
- no preview cookie but an _admin or _platform cookie present (presence only): the bridge with {ok:false, reason:'live'} and no bar. This is how the editor learns its frame shows the live store after 'See the live store' or an exit.

(3) New components/preview/bridge-core.js: plain module, window and document passed in, no React. It holds the whole protocol; components/preview/PreviewBridge.js becomes a thin useEffect wrapper that calls it. v1 messages for the legacy Designer are unchanged. v2 starts after 'storeasy:editor:hello' {v:2}:
- ready {v:2, state, ok, reason?, unfinished:[section ids from [data-unfinished]]};
- capture-phase interception while v2 is active: every anchor click, form submit and button submit is prevented;
- pick {type:'storeasy:pick', doc, sectionId, kind, field, offset} from the closest [data-doc], [data-section-id] and [data-field]; offset is the clicked block child's index inside a rich text field;
- select {type:'storeasy:select', sectionId} from the parent outlines and scrolls;
- refresh reloads and restores scroll and selection through sessionStorage (try/catch).

(4) Preview-only attributes, rendered only when ctx.preview: data-doc on Header (doc_header; doc_announcement on the bar), Footer (doc_footer) and main (the route's document id from the getter); data-field on editable text in HeroSection, the HomeSections renderers and ContentPage with exactly validate's field paths: title, subtitle, buttons.N.label, body.N (text section paragraphs), items.N.question, items.N.answer. HeroSection selects by data-section-id; v1 data-sec='hero' stays.

(5) components/PreviewBanner.js: 'You're seeing your unpublished changes.' and 'See the live store' to /api/preview?exit=1&to=<client pathname>. When the route's document is offline (state.offline), add: 'This page is offline. Publishing it brings it back.'

(6) New components/preview/EditThisPage.js (client, usePathname): rendered only with no preview and an _admin or _platform cookie present; links to /admin/editor?path=<pathname>.

